            "description": "Agentic search finds the right documents about twice as often as classical retrieval, but it can cost 100-1000x more per query and take minutes instead of milliseconds. Most agents burn 30-50% of their total tokens on search alone, before the real task even begins. Here's why SID.AI argues the fix is offloading search to a reinforcement-learning-trained sub-agent instead of the main agent.",
