    "transcript": {
        "duration": 52.060001373291016,
        "text": "AI agents burn 30-50% of their tokens just searching. Search is quietly eating your agent budget. Agentic search finds the right documents about twice as often as classical retrieval, but it costs roughly 100-1000 times more per query and takes minutes instead of milliseconds. Agents are spending 30-50% of their total tokens on search alone, almost all of it up front before the real task even starts. SID.AI's pitch is to stop making the main agent search, hand it to a sub-agent and train that model with reinforcement learning. The argument is that classic pipelines – rewrite, retrieve, re-rank – bake every decision in ad design time, so a re-ranker that knows the results are bad still can't act. If you want the link, just comment search and I'll send it to you.",
